{
  "engine": "eleven_v4",
  "clips": [
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Ask the people in the front row if this was a happy life. They’ll tell you yes. Then they’ll ask how much time you have.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/9abbd3d2d024567624a8951eaaed7d77ea1d2c04762bcadcc59a09dc77b33f57.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7440,
      "sha256": "74d55f2aeefa7fbb2553ccbd100b597a2165c99cb3f2edaf0168bd1f097b85fa"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Listen to this room. Somebody just laughed at a memory and then apologized. Please, keep the laugh.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/dd316ef0fa2372ba2dca3243349bcf407d2a41218d204eb4d7a04dd821436ec2.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7440,
      "sha256": "de082706349b68b7c66b2347845b12bb82f913dfdd4362dfc98d93140e2e696a"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Some people spend a lifetime saying, “When things settle down.” Look at this room. Things finally settled down.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/00e902e373a98a3954638cddc3ee55936bd2afc4076b3459d8e5dd793afb4d7f.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8000,
      "sha256": "be482faccad5dd1f083adf298f3e22dd91b0d9c7a1055809b98659a28bbff348"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "There was a wedding. There was a promise. And the person we came to bury broke it with somebody else.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/0266e5a754ef9338174ce131ffa6317b7380649241a6855b0a84c85c4fb073d7.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6800,
      "sha256": "61b32ae310cc154fcd766f2dc50684b808c61d0971d9f1d00668865dec5bc3a9"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "There were two people in that marriage. Then there were three. The one who broke the vow is still alive.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/bdc881462bfbc498b35405e120af81d046cee4f4a4847e2a43cae9b71c2e495f.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7280,
      "sha256": "710b7a1e96ac3b5e7c11316add2ea9e1f57eb82d96a2413cd6c7573408d07d25"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "The marriage ended before this life did. Funny how a signature can settle the house and leave the heart exactly where it was.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/f55150d92be1c9b2f5fda9b22f564a3b9fbaee5a0572e0ef73fec9b7c4de41b8.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8080,
      "sha256": "6452c6e3262b26ab396ed2285c9d2ccd17d06c18d972009a4a0bbe929f653e4f"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "There’s a word in the wedding vows that nobody hears properly until a day like today. It’s the word “until.”",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/ffedb1f1a1fc4cfdaceeee1cab7ad9357be855552435806c51039bc38500ce75.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7200,
      "sha256": "5cd48d2d17c6761cb6d91042ea01e7d7466ab95fa0a94c7c0802979ba4cfc46d"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Their daughter stayed close. Everybody keeps asking what this life amounted to. Ask her. See how long it takes her to answer.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/8d937a875d99e2755b75bb4484588eb7984fb50c0397786dbb676553f36e3ab6.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8560,
      "sha256": "87dc5b87e6514fe9098f18c03967552eeb3ee3104f9f4cb97b87372676d9127a"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Through all of it, one son stayed close. When someone asks what this life amounted to, I’d start with him.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/f8f5d7c9ca9be1e3e3dc13356b0b9f74033e524aa1343bf3b7136ffbdc9bffb7.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7680,
      "sha256": "31f02d1064ec2242cd6dd7b3acd639d3922d54d748f004c3b40cc34aabf7995a"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "There was a daughter, too. The distance between them is part of her story to tell, if she ever chooses to.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/878eeb073ea739b74425c78f6cc3bb7cc2b76f6ad3f4cd45d4787bf49775d1d1.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6800,
      "sha256": "cf8413a5954c543ba560e7e42e807cf62a79f9faaae8f463dd483509972f4735"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "There was a son, too. They grew apart. Imagine all the things that never quite made it into a phone call.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/7b5b16da36cdc0f06ef3e7d20356febe8ad9b72c63914d87d1e01855f8fc95c4.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7200,
      "sha256": "1782fcec48f4715e945540be0a4d786c764409658c6d64945257aac9761ce4d4"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "People tell me to keep these things short. I’ll be brief. I won’t tidy up somebody’s whole life just to make it fit on this card.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/64fc3dbc52cc3d248ef7a4c380c3b6eb1bd15c414da728c7eba6e6078361859b.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7680,
      "sha256": "d6a65f230208b15925dcc7b8d1194503acbd43c7936e69054d2dc182e00f327e"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "You can read every date on this program and still miss the whole person. Someone who was there can tell it better.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/e22ccc2b939c0ce1ee2994644010a3e4de8b15d1f4ad4fda28378def4169fe4d.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7120,
      "sha256": "0124c381e1b2321f33f1c6d19972381838349ff652f280c5760187704c94ec7d"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "I’m going to leave a little room here. Love can make a person stand up. It can also make it impossible to speak.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/6e687a3621a8ecc7cb7df466a485d93ed751da7f5744e052f9e41af18768a0cb.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7760,
      "sha256": "68cc6ef8460ef1e1b883511e739b8228050cdc2d57f6aa2fb47ab94d33c97620"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Take a moment. Think of the person you nearly called on the way here. When you get outside, make the call.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/611194d3cadf84c6b8dcb8293ee853645152f9deae52d439fe84f3429dc67d3f.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7200,
      "sha256": "b9eb94b12c064988e76fcfd1bc3a4b456325c8c913a4b33a1e8124d87ae1a0f0"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up once. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/0df63df9e5fe3ad3fcf62241693fac32ca9e37a9f42bbaaf99f9352c3b98d669.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7840,
      "sha256": "16b2282cb9744227ef90e7f096b232ec60fb5789f407862c6d97fc325b293cb6"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up twice. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/adab4de72cb0bafeed535ab1252536b413372bc443c6f1dc3dac6e9863b84fd5.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7920,
      "sha256": "fa312f31abc6b65f9fe9ef2681b1983f8f0d7ff93a0e308f1af61a98f8911ae8"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up three times. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/8105cac62ff56068e0212e729a2e3e785d2c2838476c79ce61fb4b80eca87e6b.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8240,
      "sha256": "9c7c18715b2b8f3b7985643d6fc0369a04ace4d911e0913cd2f397a9f544bfa0"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up four times. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/489a0746d15d5c3cdb5ae4324dcec1679f5b55d97129c6c95ffbaa64d3442249.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8320,
      "sha256": "0f62ef193bfb9abd1579240347ec7adf833dd706555bfd165ef442e6883cd12b"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up five times. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/ba161a4a48a76966502c8f6e2efaad1a9392019ec533fd7da2becc4971d3f962.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8480,
      "sha256": "8470aa288da7fa76e551eba432801858a5cf25cb0e7a501efe2bc2050971ef78"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up six times. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/4b0cb4168aedb5e69deef18c49c7325143fc250a74f6a02e89f960565f69e3ac.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8320,
      "sha256": "35d6ddca55f807298e8806166f4e4e5e06725680cf20c10080101067e373e804"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku",
      "text": "You cheated on me. I practiced saying that without crying. Look at me. I still can’t.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/8afc5d28da35f51f3b5cfa8036e7566d1914d5571c3875c72eae74de79fb13db.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7360,
      "sha256": "d61d528a9d23f6e9239c790d1cc36a59b9b552a4d4a2e8070ef0708878a0c1ab"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku",
      "text": "It was me. I cheated. I thought I could stand up here and just say I missed you. I do. Both things are true.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/9d71b34790b761d324a00f985c743bcc499889368bf6bf03c875863280161c04.mp3",
      "durationMs": 9440,
      "sha256": "ef3e7d88c87f26a85e3e6101356df3fc2ae17cec859cb6362d384fb4987523c8"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku",
      "text": "We got divorced. I thought that meant I’d already done the losing part. Then I walked in here.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/4927479684eeb2942a999becbf224394bc847039693e558d1a19a22b26450cce.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6640,
      "sha256": "6e2a13eab6e0cd09148223f36a7f7fa2a9a643d8cca5ae00677e91ac0dfed993"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku",
      "text": "We said “until death.” I had the words memorized. I never practiced what to say the day after.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/ed99daabdb93d1d3217871db41f2c2815ff36afabea0a9e2ed564be6f77c5d1e.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7520,
      "sha256": "5b8357c02b4d92d26d8fb77016ebb193a6d068273e031d318048a40a7d1e15f3"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "The neighbor Jules carried out of the fire survived. Jules died of smoke inhalation at 46.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/41ed97976b066ac0116171d6bfe5d17508adfc8872617a305e90f77e1a0a9833.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6560,
      "sha256": "dc27ad5ee758d0192ce6474a048e0c3011c0537752485d0e4d9c7a8a654e6bdd"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_kore",
      "voice": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL",
      "text": "I kept his seat until the lights went down. At the next recital, he was there before me.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/ceebb4b4fb45e1d2eb2498b4aae3baf0773e816a959ca2b849ccfc282c233c65.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5360,
      "sha256": "61827ee4911f3713dd23f142e0eb9d9048cfea099e4bee2129371986f8c49f1b"
    },
    {
      "cast": "am_fenrir",
      "voice": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Four months without a call. I still have the voicemail that starts, “Papa, it’s me.”",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/80893328930e314b04cb10f50799da2ffe756ab13630f94db4a42ff2fb1b27c1.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6560,
      "sha256": "ffe4182a45396add8d101d5e70b4e1e61b3acef8d5cb1d6828cbe71b581f7081"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bf_emma",
      "voice": "Xb7hH8MSUJpSbSDYk0k2",
      "text": "Everyone asks me about the fire. I miss the days he came over with bread.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/efa66d121f17caad4d5763fbd1a42ee9b6967571acb2c0c5452c9cfb48e4ef97.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5040,
      "sha256": "cfbc5b8dc763a47a1f5e4e478be7a79dfe06db84e423a4571425c85e9142f5e4"
    },
    {
      "cast": "am_puck",
      "voice": "bIHbv24MWmeRgasZH58o",
      "text": "He said, “I was wrong,” in front of the whole team. Then he let me speak.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/7e803385802a32e24c4e73e2a6244b0b7cf5e4d63611d203441cf7d3d40c3a7d.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5840,
      "sha256": "dead3a33638ade1b7ba4e82d8c99de6f2cdc07f9a6d5a08fb652f2b61c4f8a61"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Jules died of heart failure at 58.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/ee0e92d24c94290acca7d033e601b8ed72bce54430e22af908847432166630a9.mp3",
      "durationMs": 2960,
      "sha256": "298300b046ae5e7053304a78bfe1d0c1a142e14bebba800d7f5274aa3469db68"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_kore",
      "voice": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL",
      "text": "He missed my recital. At the hospital he pulled up a chair for me. I stayed.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/caf311b723a55b06486098ddbc8f1f36457fcc309e30ac87869288aa2615cb31.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5600,
      "sha256": "6ae79f4def08afc6cb7364d420d97c70eebb0ad7943f93062466f7fb5c090eca"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "At 90, Louis died in an accident.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/b876634efc7ed914a110655d76619250b7eb1e4ced66fba15fd3a5f0dc706a02.mp3",
      "durationMs": 3120,
      "sha256": "c5e1bcda518d5935b25489a6454324f2738428cd8a61976356cd8c455ae10de6"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku",
      "text": "The telephone rang while the soup went cold. I was still waiting for you at nightfall.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/37d20edbaaa33df37c7777033e9b9c9cb4da498da31e6d5d6e0a119fb07369b2.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5600,
      "sha256": "49930fa01cfb467a22fd12a458b0e2df318c2666a6913917f337111d6b95f080"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bf_emma",
      "voice": "Xb7hH8MSUJpSbSDYk0k2",
      "text": "At 51, Louis kept one evening free at home. I kept the envelope with my name in pencil.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/72dcb9c1b9a0e02a17cead2d0009ebffdea376095c2539b09b793a65585ff761.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6640,
      "sha256": "78975f56b9853e9e72dea50538af5b1e47d0f620bffa4fade66ff690950ffb24"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_bella",
      "voice": "cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9",
      "text": "You were 90 when you took the late meeting. The little blue chair by the door was empty.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/2cdd89877f41cfb4ddc894322dd5f8eb84ea2ab88d1b2edb7932891d3bc7d968.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5280,
      "sha256": "fa72cdb80f42b4a787c5b8bba43b2a95cce9a8ea11c04e742db44e06214e19b5"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "We remember Louis, who died of cancer at 82.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/33f29e9d3f09aa618326e7927894595baa57eafa98c355db96fe010aafc7f47b.mp3",
      "durationMs": 3680,
      "sha256": "5eeca51db8329ffbcaaa6d4a08f4912ec85e6c4af53932a8bfd313aeed1e807a"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku",
      "text": "At 66, Louis took the late meeting. The brass key was still under the flowerpot.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/2499fc11645d45f22e5e30a8ad7b69213374baf41d0a3384e6ab2cce79a120f7.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6000,
      "sha256": "748ffdd8efbe0a7f0b7940176639d3d49224050914c5d8abfac83b79f68004d6"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bf_emma",
      "voice": "Xb7hH8MSUJpSbSDYk0k2",
      "text": "You were 41 when you asked for help. The telephone rang while the soup went cold.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/951647851adcaef6cac819a596ae8354b2b9cfa12fb7ef3d95b52f864b33246a.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5760,
      "sha256": "c469ee55b7a3a15e8897694ecbc7a028b22c6c513e32ea6801c896764a275d50"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_bella",
      "voice": "cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9",
      "text": "That little blue chair by the door was empty. But you stayed with me, Louis.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/85b6c6ce075c37eddcc768714cf4f9a833dcc6eb6886c8d79e3bba1d4b30f7f1.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5040,
      "sha256": "8e4559b80c82503b5e1af2cff7029a7acd965a446218fec71c176307bc7a1108"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Louis died of cancer at 89.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/05f2da952e76d95d8e061a9324a0fd29c953cf385ae18db03bb4291174e2a829.mp3",
      "durationMs": 2640,
      "sha256": "745b7a79c370fb0dabda475cb5d320ca5169b69f4889a4dd710f49909bb7aecb"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku",
      "text": "I still have the paper ticket from the last train. That was the evening you stayed with me.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/cf049f460f3aa49a79442254d944e83cd9b54fdb7a7c1cc0945a44d1c4777170.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5040,
      "sha256": "1a408e51b78ff2b82f3ea7830c910956e6b9fefe72e85914e4489d52b93b054a"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_bella",
      "voice": "cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9",
      "text": "You were 66 when you kept one evening free at home. The little blue chair by the door was empty.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/dffcf6c6e71486126741d16be28eed65fc352b881f15eace44ddf9c33d4d6a9d.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6400,
      "sha256": "02d45d5826c8bc2bbba623dc8e94ffb8c65468629144dd93d9a760de8be10d47"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bf_emma",
      "voice": "Xb7hH8MSUJpSbSDYk0k2",
      "text": "You were 36 when you took the late meeting. I kept the envelope with my name in pencil.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/b58af4902cf578fafa35e13513b1f88778416c78d17a3bfe00cbe1e53c333236.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5680,
      "sha256": "5b6b986281b7df453c1c58cf08ec27a958c4bd081077c777a994d79b66daf0d0"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "At 83, Louis died of heart disease.",
